      "writtenOn": "2026-08-14T05:21:54Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This is a genuine requirement for IBM systems, where certain types of dumps can be quite large in size (often exceeding 500 MB). Once support for this functionality is available, we will have a corresponding client implementation in place.\n\nFor testing purposes, I developed a client that retrieves the dump in multiple 1 MB chunks. After all the chunks are downloaded, the client stitches them together to reconstruct the complete file. I have validated this approach, and it works as expected.",
      "parentUuid": "308b49c2_fb80d7d2",
      "revId": "a2121ff037fc22eec20e68e58a209d7df0930f4c",
